Complete the Jinja2 / HuggingFace `transformers` chat-template runtime features missing from upstream:
- global builtins: `dict`, `zip`, `enumerate`, `len`, `str`, `int`, `float`, `bool`, `list`, `min`, `max`,
  `sum`, `abs`, `round`, `sorted`, `reversed`, `any`, and `all`;
- separate filter dispatch (`value_t::get_filters()`) from member lookup (`value_t::get_builtins()`), so
  object filters (`default`, `length`, `string`, `tojson`, `dictsort`, `list`, `safe`) never shadow dict
  keys such as `param.default`;
- filters and tests: `tojson(sort_keys=...)`, `from_json`, distinct `select`/`reject` vs
  `selectattr`/`rejectattr`, `le` test, `value_object` in `is iterable`, `sum` on arrays, `list` on
  strings/objects, `replace` with `count`, and `str.join`;
- methods and language: dict `update`/`pop`/`setdefault`/`copy`/`clear`, string `find`/`rfind`/`splitlines`/
  `removeprefix`/`removesuffix`/`count`, tuple/list `startswith`/`endswith`, negative string indexing,
  whitespace `split()`/`rsplit()`, list `extend`/`insert`/`remove`/`index`/`count`/`copy`/`clear`,
  `{% do ... %}` (`jinja2.ext.do`), and `{% for ch in str %}`.
